ADF 2027 — Direction
Made entirely in code. No stock footage, no generated video, no generated images.

TYPEFACE
  Archivo (variable roman, weight 100–900, width 62–125)
  Omnibus-Type · https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/archivo
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 · the licence text ships beside the font in fonts/OFL.txt
  Used for every word in the film.

SOUND
  Score and foley are synthesised in this project (mix.py) with numpy and scipy:
  kick, closed hat, rim, bass, marimba, glockenspiel, vibraphone, sine glide, and the print
  foley (ruling pen, block snap, letterpress clack, guillotine snick, paper slap and slide,
  numeral thunk, rubber stamp, carriage return). No sample libraries, no recordings,
  no third-party audio of any kind.

PICTURE
  Drawn frame by frame with Canvas 2D in this project (film.js), captured headless and
  encoded with ffmpeg. Lemo-Opuscar supplies the render and audio tooling
  (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, code MIT); none of its demo material,
  artwork or music is in this film.

CONTENT
  Every figure, name and quoted phrase is from the source deck, "Atlanta Design Festival 2027 —
  Direction for the twentieth year", September 2026, supplied by the client. The seventeen
  organisations are named as set type, not as logos or marks. The film carries no third-party
  trademark, photograph, footage, map or dataset.

  The weekly sales bars are the increments behind the deck's cumulative sales curve (slide 03).
  They reproduce the three figures the deck states: $1,420 (10%) in at four weeks out,
  $8,855 (60%) in event week, 78% in the final two weeks, $14,685 total on 407 tickets.

